        "y1": 0.6333588761174969
      },
      "text": "remains ﬁxed.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.424617094017094,
        "y0": 0.6141724137931035,
        "x1": 0.4280837606837607,
        "y1": 0.6204891443167305
      },
      "text": "4",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07378632478632478,
        "y0": 0.6333959131545339,
        "x1": 0.4841709401709402,
        "y1": 0.7185338441890166
      },
      "text": "The speciﬁc growth rates became maximal at the entry of the exponential stage and remained constant throughout the particular stage (Fig. 1B, 2B, and 3A). The values did not significantly differ among the various gassing regimens (0.22 to 0.25 h 1; doubling times of 2.8 to 3.1 h) (Table 3). However, the qCH",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07378632478632478,
        "y0": 0.7036385696040869,
        "x1": 0.48418290598290603,
        "y1": 0.8019399744572159
      },
      "text": "was not constant. Speciﬁc methane-forming activities initially increased to a maximum and declined thereafter. The decline occurred concomitant with the decrease in the dissolved hydrogen partial pressures, resulting from the increasing hydrogen uptake rates by the growing biomass (Fig. 1 and 2 and Table 3). Apparently, the physiology of the cells continuously changed, even at a constant growth rate.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.09588376068376069,
        "y0": 0.7125121328224777,
        "x1": 0.09935042735042734,
        "y1": 0.7188288633461046
      },
      "text": "4",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07378632478632478,
        "y0": 0.8019770114942528,
        "x1": 0.48415555555555556,
        "y1": 0.8730676883780332
      },
      "text": "After exponential growth, the cells entered the linear phase. During this stage, the speciﬁc growth rates and speciﬁc methane-forming activities, calculated by using the equations S.5 and S.6, respectively, in the supplemental material(1), decreased in parallel (Fig. 1B and 2B). Moreover, qCH",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.423034188034188,
        "y0": 0.8581724137931035,
        "x1": 0.47384957264957267,
        "y1": 0.872183908045977
      },
      "text": "-versus-",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.41956752136752135,
        "y0": 0.8670459770114942,
        "x1": 0.423034188034188,
        "y1": 0.8733614303959132
      },
      "text": "4",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.07378632478632478,
        "y0": 0.8722209450830141,
        "x1": 0.484174358974359,
        "y1": 0.9283780332056194
      },
      "text": "plots showed the direct proportional relationship as expected from equation S.8 (Fig. 1C, 2C, and 3B). The slope of the plots, which equals the reciprocal of the speciﬁc growth yield (equation S.8), varied with the dissolved hydrogen partial pressure",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "picture",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5554786324786325,
        "y0": 0.38201021711366534,
        "x1": 0.8836837606837608,
        "y1": 0.7958033205619413
      },
      "text": null,
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5148102564102564,
        "y0": 0.8006513409961686,
        "x1": 0.9252136752136753,
        "y1": 0.9063141762452107
      },
      "text": "FIG. 3. Relationship between the speciﬁc rates of methanogenesis and speciﬁc growth rates during the lag (A), linear (B), and exponential growth phases. M. thermautotrophicus was cultured in 2.5 (A) and 1.5 (B) liters of mineral medium at a constant gassing rate of 428 ml min 1 in 80% H2–20% CO2 (vol/vol). Measurements started 5 h (A) and 8 h (B) after adjustment of the gassing rates. In the inset of Fig. 3A, the ln(OD600) is plotted versus the squared time after inoculation. Lag ( ), exponential (Œ), and linear (}) growth stages are as indicated. ex, speciﬁc growth rate during the exponential phase;",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5148119658119659,
        "y0": 0.9040983397190294,
        "x1": 0.5344735042735043,
